From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 11:02:22 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Reject an entity on X out of the bucket's own extents array

Chunk.scanSliceForEntity was 7.07% of the server thread in self time, and the
six comparisons it performs are not what that time is. Reading a candidate's
boundingBoxMinX means dereferencing an Entity - 86 fields, somewhere else
entirely in the heap - so a dense crowd costs a cache miss per candidate and
the arithmetic waits on memory.

Each bucket now carries a double[] of its entities' X extents, interleaved
minX,maxX, parallel to the bucket list. The scan decides the X overlap out of
that contiguous array and only touches the Entity for a candidate that
survives. X is the axis the buckets spread over, so it is the selective one,
and the test is the first two comparisons of the full intersection - anything
that passes goes on to the same check it always did.

The array rides the existing choke points: bucketAdd appends, a new
bucketRemove takes the two sites that dropped an entity from a bucket and
keeps both in step, and updateEntityBucket - already called from
setEntityBoundingBox for every move - refreshes the extents on the path where
the entity stays in its bucket. Entity.athenaBucketSlot records where in the
bucket an entity sits so that refresh needs no search. Removal shifts rather
than swapping the last entry into the hole, so the order queries see, which is
the order collisions resolve in, is unchanged.

A stale extent loses a collision silently rather than crashing, so the bucket
audit now checks every entry against the entity it mirrors, and the slot too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java
index b877fd9302227c586f04db88fd4a02973944dbb9..3e2317d287c1b4b74dc7dd7c9e63f33b282ef3cf 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/AthenaIndexAudit.java
@@ -248,9 +248,35 @@ public final class AthenaIndexAudit {
                         continue;
                     }
 
+                    // Athena - the X extents array beside this bucket. A stale entry makes the
+                    // scan reject a candidate it should have returned, which loses a collision
+                    // silently, so it is checked value by value against the entity it mirrors.
+                    double[] xs = chunk.auditBucketExtents(slice, b);
+                    int slot = 0;
+
                     for (Entity entity : buckets[b]) {
                         ++found;
 
+                        // Athena start
+                        if (entity.athenaBucketSlot != slot) {
+                            report("entity " + entity.getId() + " sits at index " + slot + " of bucket " + b
+                                    + " but records slot " + entity.athenaBucketSlot);
+                        }
+
+                        if (xs != null && (slot << 1) + 1 < xs.length) {
+                            if (xs[slot << 1] != entity.boundingBoxMinX || xs[(slot << 1) | 1] != entity.boundingBoxMaxX) {
+                                report("entity " + entity.getId() + " at index " + slot + " of bucket " + b
+                                        + " spans X " + entity.boundingBoxMinX + ".." + entity.boundingBoxMaxX
+                                        + " but the extents say " + xs[slot << 1] + ".." + xs[(slot << 1) | 1]);
+                            }
+                        } else if (xs != null) {
+                            report("bucket " + b + " of slice " + slice + " holds " + buckets[b].size()
+                                    + " entities but its extents array only has room for " + (xs.length >> 1));
+                        }
+
+                        ++slot;
+                        // Athena end
+
                         if (entity.athenaBucket != b) {
                             report("entity " + entity.getId() + " is in bucket " + b + " but records " + entity.athenaBucket);
                         }
